  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.6.0 - The archival output is proven rather than described, and it names two more profiles. A pinned veraPDF 1.30.4 gate runs on every push and once a week (compliance.yml), cross-checked by Apache PDFBox preflight and Ghostscript, with the machine-readable reports kept as an artifact; validate-pdfa.py reads the report instead of the word PASS and refuses a validator older than the pin. PDF/A-2u and -3u join the three level-B profiles, the output intent can be the caller's own ICC profile (written verbatim, checked as an ICC profile before a byte is written), and a PDF/A-3 result associates every embedded file through /AF with a stated relationship. Beyond the archive: a page can state an opacity and a blend mode, a document's fonts can be read without opening them, a merge or an edit reads each source once instead of twice (a 100 MB merge allocates 104.2 MB instead of 204.2 MB), and configuration registration is trim- and Native AOT-compatible. Details: https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SharpCorePDF/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
